<title>ITALY: Italy offers 40.75 trln lire of BOTs for sale.</title>
<headline>Italy offers 40.75 trln lire of BOTs for sale.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1996-09-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian treasury said it was offering 40.75 trillion lire of short term bills (BOT), replacing 41.75 trillion lire of expiring paper.</p>
<p>A Treasury statement said it would offer:</p>
<p>* 13.0 trillion lire of three-month BOTs.</p>
<p>* 13.25 trillion lire of six-month paper.</p>
<p>* 14.50 trillion lire of one-year bills.</p>
<p>Subscriptions close at 1100 GMT on September 25.</p>
<p>The treasury added that it would offer 2.5 trillion lire of two-year zero couponed certificates (CTZ) with subscriptions for that sale also closing at 1100 GMT, September 25.</p>
</text>
